<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ns/pbm#"
     xml:base="https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ns/pbm"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:terms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ns/pbm#">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ns/pbm/1.0.0"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o-20130430"/>
        <terms:abstract xml:lang="en">The Provenance of Biological Material Ontology (PBM-O) expresses the Provenance of Biological Material (PBM) structures using the OWL 2 Web Ontology Language. The PBM structures are specializations of the provenance structures defined in W3C PROV-DM and are used together with the Common Provenance Model (CPM) to represent the provenance of biological material, such as samples and the activities performed on them. PBM-O is an extension of PROV-O.</terms:abstract>
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-25</terms:created>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">PBM-O provides IRIs, labels, and definitions for the terms of the PBM structures, so that these terms can be referenced from provenance documents expressed in PROV-N, PROV-JSON, PROV-XML, or RDF. In this version the ontology serves primarily as a vocabulary: it declares the PBM classes and aligns them with PROV-O. The minimum cardinality restrictions it contains document mandatory properties of the PBM structures but, under the open-world semantics of OWL, they do not validate data. Constraints for checking conformance and further features are planned for future versions.</terms:description>
        <terms:license rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">Provenance of Biological Material Ontology (PBM-O)</terms:title>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>pbm</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ns/pbm#</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Following PROV-O (Section 3.1), the PROV-DM attribute prov:type is expressed in RDF with rdf:type; PBM-O therefore does not declare prov:type. PROV-N, PROV-JSON, and PROV-XML keep prov:type unchanged, e.g. prov:type=&apos;pbm:sample&apos;. Each PBM type value (e.g. pbm:sample) is declared as a class equivalent to the corresponding PBM-O class (e.g. pbm:Sample), so RDF produced from PROV-N/PROV-JSON by standard PROV tooling is classified correctly. New RDF should use the capitalized class names.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ns/cpm#"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.commonprovenancemodel.org/ontologies/known-issues/"/>
        <owl:versionInfo xml:lang="en">1.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


